 "title": "Lake Powell's Shrinking Waters",
 "cat": "geography",
 "emoji": "🏜️",
 "sentences": [
  "Lake Powell has hit record-low water levels.",
  "By September 2026, the reservoir dropped to 3,517.24 feet.",
  "A meager winter snowpack across the Upper Colorado Basin fueled this decline.",
  "The lake barely stays above the elevation needed for hydroelectric power.",
  "Authorities are now releasing water from other reservoirs to stabilize the dam.",
  "This megadrought continues to strain water resources for 40 million people."
